CLOUDFLARE MIGRATION PLAN

QuestAcademy - architecture, implementation phases, validation, cutover, and rollback

Repository: Orsnoire/FightSchool, default branch main

Recommended production URL: https://questacademy.bookwyrminteractive.studio

Platform: Cloudflare Pages + Workers + Durable Objects; Neon retained

Assessment mode: Read-only; no repository or Cloudflare account changes made

Planning date: 17 September 2026

Decision: Change the canonical address now to https://questacademy.bookwyrminteractive.studio (not .studo). A dedicated hostname materially lowers migration risk and leaves the apex domain free for other content. Do not introduce the former /QuestAcademy path as a production dependency; add it only as an optional redirect after the new deployment passes acceptance.

1. Executive Recommendation

Adopt a staged migration with the frontend and backend isolated behind one same-origin subdomain. Keep Neon PostgreSQL during the first migration. Move live combat coordination to a Durable Object per combat session. Replace the Replit-only object-storage signing path before leaving Replit. Preserve the current host until the Cloudflare release has passed functional, load, security, and rollback tests.

