10. Manual Cloudflare Account Actions

No Cloudflare account connector is configured, so these actions remain manual and must be completed by an authorized account owner.

Confirm BookwyrmInteractive.studio is an active Cloudflare zone and inventory all DNS records before changing anything.

Create the staging and production API Worker services. Deploy the Durable Object class in a backward-compatible migration before routing sockets to it.

If Hyperdrive is selected, create staging and production configurations pointed at Neon; use conservative pool settings and cache-disabled behavior for sensitive data.

Create the Pages project from the GitHub repository with the approved build command and dist/public output. Configure separate preview and production variables.

Bind the Pages project to the API Worker through API_SERVICE. Bind the backend Worker to COMBAT_SESSIONS and the chosen database/object services.

Upload required secrets with Wrangler or the dashboard. Verify the deploy fails when declared secrets are absent.

Add questacademy.bookwyrminteractive.studio as the Pages custom domain. Resolve any existing DNS record conflict only after ownership review.

Set SSL/TLS to Full (strict), verify certificate issuance, enable production logs/traces, and record rollback operators.

After acceptance, add an optional permanent redirect from the former /QuestAcademy URL to the subdomain. Do not let the redirect capture unrelated paths.

